  "rules": [
    "the command from the app's page: \"grain pair --app <slug> --owner <address> --genesis <16 hex>\" (the SDK's syntax; the three fields are the protocol's): the app's slug (3-32 of [a-z0-9-], not starting with '-'), the owner's Bech32m address (any kind; its prefix names the network, its id is the offer's owner) and the first 8 bytes of the genesis hash in lower-case hex; a reader takes the three flags once each in any order, with white space free, and nothing else",
    "PairingOffer is Borsh {version: u8 = 2, hrp: String (\"salt\" | \"tsalt\" | \"dsalt\"), genesis: [u8;8] the first 8 bytes of the genesis hash, key: [u8;32] the server key (a valid Ed25519 key, not of small order), nonce: [u8;16] random, slug: String, owner: [u8;20] the owner's account, proof: [u8;64], name: String (the server's, at most 32 characters, none of Unicode Cc, Cf, U+2028, U+2029; may be empty), created_at: u64 Unix ms, expires_at: u64 Unix ms with created_at < expires_at <= created_at + 30 minutes}; nothing in it is secret, and nothing is signed but the proof; a reader refuses trailing bytes",
    "proof = ServerKeyProof.proof (24-app-studio §2): Ed25519 by the key over BLAKE3-derive_key(\"Salarium grain server v1\", Borsh((genesis_hash [32], slug: String, owner [20]))) — the full genesis hash, not the 8 bytes the offer names; the wallet sends it as it is in ConfigureGrain (tag 39) and keeps it for the calls that keep the key",
    "link = \"salt:grain-pair?o=\" base64url without padding of Borsh(PairingOffer); white space around it is allowed; padding, spare bits, any other character or a further parameter is refused",
    "code = the first 4 bytes of BLAKE3-derive_key(\"Salarium grain pairing code v1\", Borsh(PairingOffer)) as a big-endian u32, modulo 1 000 000; code_text is its 6 digits with leading zeros in two groups of 3 separated by one space; every field, the key and the proof included, changes it",
    "fingerprint(key) = the first 4 bytes of the key in lower-case hex; server_address = the key's personal address (kind 0) on the offer's network",
    "a wallet of an account on a chain takes an offer at now when it is of form (version, unknown_network, key, slug, name, life, malformed), hrp is the chain's prefix and genesis its first 8 bytes (other_network), created_at <= now + 5 minutes (ahead), now < expires_at (expired), owner is the account (other_owner), and the proof verifies (strict Ed25519) under key for the chain's full genesis hash, slug and owner (proof), checked in that order; nothing travels to the computer, which watches the registry",
    "the slug by the registry's record (grain_get) of it: none → free (a new app made in place, the key in its ConfigureGrain); its owner not the offer's → another_account; retired → retired; its servers name the key → paired_already (nothing to sign); else own; a wallet signs for free and own only",
    "the registry's answers to the phone's ConfigureGrain (version 4 and above checks each proof itself): applied for the owner's live app; server_key_taken for a key another live app names, whoever's (\"run grain pair --new\"); not_owner for a slug another account holds; grain_retired for a retired one; unknown_grain for a free slug, which the phone registers instead (step 4 of §3a)",
    "an offer of version 1 (2026-10-19) is read for its version only: a reader says to update the SDK and run grain pair again; an offer of a version above 2 says to update the wallet; both are the refusal version"
  ],
